WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.855 --> 00:00:02.782
A plant is building a new hall.

2
00:00:03.449 --> 00:00:07.884
Packing line 3 has to move there, during the summer shutdown of 3 weeks.

3
00:00:08.893 --> 00:00:12.620
Every project walks the same road, past seven stations.

4
00:00:13.761 --> 00:00:18.022
At each station you see what happens, and what goes wrong if you skip it.

5
00:00:19.363 --> 00:00:21.859
The first station is Approach and tools.

6
00:00:22.553 --> 00:00:24.759
Here you choose how to run the project.

7
00:00:25.781 --> 00:00:29.578
The move suits a predictive approach, plan first and then run.

8
00:00:30.273 --> 00:00:31.898
The sponsor gives the mandate.

9
00:00:32.948 --> 00:00:36.501
With the approach we often use a task board and an ERP.

10
00:00:37.488 --> 00:00:42.121
Without an approach you start without a route, and everyone picks their own tools.

11
00:00:43.438 --> 00:00:45.574
The second station is the intake.

12
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.413
The request is, move line 3.

13
00:00:49.107 --> 00:00:51.475
You dig deeper to the question behind it.

14
00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:53.667
Why, and when is it done?

15
00:00:54.668 --> 00:00:58.093
The answer becomes the goal, what must be measurably different.

16
00:00:58.849 --> 00:01:03.610
After the shutdown line 3 runs in hall B, as fast as it does now.

17
00:01:04.344 --> 00:01:05.726
The sponsor decides.

18
00:01:06.763 --> 00:01:10.223
At intake we often use a project charter and a SIPOC.

19
00:01:11.326 --> 00:01:14.379
Skip the intake, and you may solve the wrong problem.

20
00:01:15.682 --> 00:01:17.331
The third station is Plan.

21
00:01:18.048 --> 00:01:21.159
You turn the goal into a plan that people believe in.

22
00:01:22.179 --> 00:01:25.279
The work, the order, the duration and the risks.

23
00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:27.860
The intro of Plan shows them.

24
00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:32.753
When planning we often use a WBS and the critical path.

25
00:01:33.737 --> 00:01:34.550
Without a plan,

26
00:01:34.758 --> 00:01:37.522
you only notice in the last week of the shutdown

27
00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.530
that the new power supply is not ready.

28
00:01:40.819 --> 00:01:43.594
The fourth station is Formats and meetings.

29
00:01:44.325 --> 00:01:45.381
The plan is ready.

30
00:01:46.102 --> 00:01:48.122
Now the group has to work together.

31
00:01:49.134 --> 00:01:53.976
Each meeting format has a purpose and participants, a duration and an output.

32
00:01:55.025 --> 00:01:58.589
With formats we often use a pre-read and a brown paper.

33
00:01:59.622 --> 00:02:03.001
Without a format a meeting just talks, with no output.

34
00:02:04.375 --> 00:02:06.024
The fifth station is Run.

35
00:02:06.781 --> 00:02:08.824
Now the project has to keep moving.

36
00:02:09.887 --> 00:02:11.292
Keep the status honest.

37
00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:15.305
The switchboard comes later than planned, so amber now.

38
00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.420
Someone asks whether line 4 can come along too.

39
00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:23.541
That becomes a change request, and the sponsor chooses.

40
00:02:24.546 --> 00:02:29.480
When running the project we often use an A3 status report and a decision log.

41
00:02:30.536 --> 00:02:35.621
Without steering you get a watermelon project, green outside and red inside.

42
00:02:36.961 --> 00:02:38.656
The sixth station is Land.

43
00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:44.044
Line 3 is in place, and now the new way of working has to stick.

44
00:02:45.046 --> 00:02:49.063
The operators get a work instruction with photos of the real line,

45
00:02:49.248 --> 00:02:50.699
and training on the floor.

46
00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.212
Then the line takes over.

47
00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:54.983
That is adoption.

48
00:02:55.662 --> 00:02:59.099
People work the new way, even when nobody is watching.

49
00:03:00.124 --> 00:03:04.838
When landing the change we often use a skills matrix and a handover checklist.

50
00:03:05.935 --> 00:03:09.650
Skip this, and the result slips away after a few months.

51
00:03:10.936 --> 00:03:12.817
The last station is Close.

52
00:03:13.532 --> 00:03:15.854
The work is done, the project is not.

53
00:03:16.906 --> 00:03:20.946
You measure the line the same way as in the baseline, from before the move.

54
00:03:21.692 --> 00:03:23.120
Then the sponsor signs.

55
00:03:24.226 --> 00:03:25.526
Then a retrospective.

56
00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.478
What do we repeat, and what do we do differently next time?

57
00:03:30.485 --> 00:03:34.328
When closing we often use a run chart and a closing report.

58
00:03:35.413 --> 00:03:38.316
Without closing nobody knows whether it worked,

59
00:03:38.525 --> 00:03:41.219
and the next project makes the same mistakes.

60
00:03:42.507 --> 00:03:44.237
This is the map of Projects.

61
00:03:44.942 --> 00:03:47.473
The seven stations lie on one road.

62
00:03:48.535 --> 00:03:51.832
First Approach and the intake, the route and the question.

63
00:03:53.031 --> 00:03:56.340
Then Plan and Formats, the plan and the teamwork.

64
00:03:57.417 --> 00:04:00.099
Then Run and Land, the work and the change.

65
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.430
Finally Close, proving and learning.

66
00:04:04.479 --> 00:04:07.184
Each station is a module with four topics.

67
00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:09.747
Start with Approach and tools.
